    description: "Found doing WI-daruz (2026-10-28). Producers emit exactly three UsageContext kinds -- call, export, library_export (AST scan of every UsageContext(...)/UsageContext.create(...) in packages/*/src; test_usage_context_kinds pins it). Eight framework usage rules name a kind no producer emits, so they match nothing:\n- cowboy.yaml (erlang): 4 rules with usage.kind ^function$ (handler init / handle|info|terminate, rest_callback, websocket_callback);\n- qt.yaml (cpp): 2 rules with ^macro$ (Q_OBJECT -> qt_class, Q_PROPERTY -> property) and 1 with ^method$ (event handlers);\n- servant.yaml (haskell): 1 rule with ^type$ (Get|Post|... route combinators).\nThe rule shapes look like they meant a SYMBOL kind (symbol_kind:) or a usage the analyzer would need to emit (Q_OBJECT as a macro usage). Per rule: rewrite to a key the matcher reads and verify on a fixture, or have the analyzer emit the usage, or delete with a note. test_usage_context_kinds::test_framework_usage_rules_name_a_produced_kind pins these eight as a shrink-only known-dead list naming this item."  # 9ed4
